    "statement": "Packed rows cost exactly the modelled bytes per coefficient on every bank; the shared word table costs its own bytes per distinct word. So the total per coefficient is the row cost plus the table cost divided by coefficient reuse, and the reduction rises with reuse rather than being a property of the representation alone. At the bottom of the measured ladder that sum exceeds what it replaces and packing is a net loss, which is the same mechanism read from the other end rather than a separate effect.",
